I would suggest playing a mix of races/roles/alignments.

Each role plays differently from every other class.  Even within a
role, changing up the race changes your play style (it's sometimes
quite subtle).

That said, if you're determined to play a race/role/alignment
combination until you ascend, I'll offer few suggestions:

sam-hum-law:  A properly played Samurai does offense better than anyone
else.

val-dwa-law:  Plus: sleepwalk the mines.  Minus: Don't even bother with
spellbooks.

ran-elf-cha:  Unlimited ammo, no penalty for poison, and damn does a
stack of blessed poisoned +7 arrows do stupid amounts of damage or
what?

bar-orc-cha:  A bit light on late-game offense.  Especially fun if you
go for style (Orcrist + elven broadsword).

tou-hum-neu:  Everyone should try for a beach gear ascension at least
once.  (only wore Hawaiian shirt, lenses, or a towel).

arc-hum-neu:  Probably the most balanced between wombat and casting of
all the role/race combinations.

